Package: luna2-client
Version: 2.2-4
Maintainer: ClusterVision
Architecture: amd64
Depends: initramfs-tools | dracut, dracut-network | initramfs-tools, shim-signed, grub-efi-amd64-signed, grub-efi-amd64-bin, mdadm, lvm2, gdisk, fdisk, lsscsi, jq, parted, dosfstools, lbzip2, aria2, efibootmgr, grepcidr, curl, openssh-server, dropbear-bin, tpm2-tools
Description: Luna node install module with lpart advanced-partitioner support
 Ships both an initramfs-tools hook and a dracut 95luna module. Ubuntu 22.04 and
 24.04 default to initramfs-tools; 25.10 and later default to dracut. The daemon
 packs with whichever the image provides, so one package covers both.
 .
 The second alternative pulls dracut's network modules, which ubuntu ships as a
 separate package. 95luna depends on dracut's 'network' module, and without it
 dracut drops the whole luna module, still exits 0, and the node boots to
 "don't know how to handle root=luna". Ordered dracut-network first because
 installing initramfs-tools on a dracut image removes dracut; on 22.04 and 24.04
 initramfs-tools is already present, so the clause is satisfied and pulls nothing.
